      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unlike set_cr0/set_cr4, the set_efer callback in kvm_x86_ops has a return value (since https://lore.kernel.org/all/20201001112954.6258-4-mlevitsk@redhat.com/) and KVM assumes that set_efer may legitimately return an error (and returns this error to userspace) in some cases.\n\nAlthough I see that in the VMX case, vmx_set_efer() should always return success with a well-behaving host [*]. But that might change in the future (although unlikely)? Also, even though currently the entire `vmx/pkvm_host.c` is VMX-specific, perhaps some parts of it could be moved to a vendor-agnostic code in the future, to support non-VMX pKVM implementations, so maybe it\u0027s better to avoid adding such VMX-specific assumptions unless really needed? WDYT?\n\n[*] In fact, it looks like this hypercall here always returns success even with a misbehaving host, since vmx_set_efer() may only return an error if CONFIG_X86_64\u003dn which is not supported by pKVM.",
